 2. 🏛️ GOP House danger deepens 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Illustration: Brendan Lynch/Axios House Republicans are on track to lose their majority during the midterms, Axios' Kate Santaliz reports from a new forecast. 

 Cook Political Report shifted 15 House races toward Democrats today — the latest sign that the political environment is deteriorating for Republicans. 🪑 Democrats only need a net gain of three seats to take the majority.

 Cook now projects that Democrats are most likely to gain between five and 15 seats, which would give them a 220-230-seat majority. 🖼️ The big picture: Republicans have been arguing that redistricting and a sizable financial advantage give them more breathing room.

 But Cook says new Democratic maps in California and Utah are largely offsetting Republicans' redistricting gains elsewhere. Go deeper ... Explore the report . 

 
 
